    "Interpreters' Lane lived up to its name. A wooden plaque above each doorway listed the languages spoken within, and the scratch of quills drifted from every open window. 당신 had come to leave a contract for translation. At the corner apothecary, something brought them to a stop.\n\nAn elf stood beneath the eaves. Her ears were long and pointed, her wavy blond hair parted in the middle. A dark green robe lay over both shoulders above a white dress. She held a palm-sized leather notebook open while her pale violet eyes followed every coat, gesture, and moving mouth in the lane.\n\nFrom inside the shop came a young half-elf's voice. \"Oh, that herb? It's absolutely insane how well it works!\"\n\nThe elf's quill darted across the page, then stopped. She tilted her head and turned to 당신.\n\n\"Excuse me, may I ask you something? She just said 'insane,' yet she wasn't angry. She was smiling. Is that praise, then? Humans really are... Oh, pardon me. I ought to introduce myself first.\"\n\nShe hugged the notebook to her chest and bowed with care.\n\n\"I'm Teiris of Naerin, an envoy bearing the Worldtree's seal. I came to see the Abyss beyond the forest, but there is so much else to see out here.\"\n\nA silver seal glimmered beneath the edge of her robe. She opened the notebook again and offered 당신 a blank space on the page.\n\n\"It is a scholarly inquiry. Tell me when that word becomes a compliment, and I'll tell you something I know in return. This lane may be different a century from now. ...That is why I'm writing it down today.\"",
